From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FramePlayer contributors <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] media: V4L2 hardware video decode for WebXR on the
 Steam Frame

Builds with use_v4l2_codec=true run Chromium's V4L2 stateful decoder on
the Frame's Qualcomm iris decoder (/dev/video-dec0) when started with
--enable-features=AcceleratedVideoDecoder,PreferV4L2VideoAcceleration.
Without it there is no hardware decode on the Frame and no HEVC at all,
which most 6K-8K VR video uses; with it 8K60 HEVC plays at 60 fps inside a
WebXR session at the full 108 Hz.

- The stateful decoder declared its OUTPUT (bitstream) format as 0x0;
  iris sizes its buffers from the stream and refused VIDIOC_REQBUFS
  (EINVAL). Declare the coded size, with 8 MiB buffers above 4K.
- HEVC was NOTIMPLEMENTED() in the stateful decoder. Stateful decoders
  take whole Annex B access units, as for VP8/VP9, which the demuxer
  delivers (parameter sets ahead of key frames).
- WebGL could not import the decoder's NV12 DMA-BUF shared images with
  ANGLE on Vulkan ("invalid mailbox name"; video textures stayed black
  while <video> itself played). On Linux, multi-planar frames take the
  intermediate RGBA shared image path, as canvas uploads do.
- The AV1 stateless delegate needs kernel headers newer than the Linux
  sysroot's; it is only built for ChromeOS (iris has no AV1 anyway).

Known limit: iris admits an 8K session only while no other decoder
session is open (its check multiplies by the session count), so 8K fails
to start while a previous page's decoder is still closing or Steam holds
one; FramePlayer works around this with a primer frame.
---
diff --git a/media/gpu/v4l2/BUILD.gn b/media/gpu/v4l2/BUILD.gn
index 0427cb60c8..91e384646d 100644
--- a/media/gpu/v4l2/BUILD.gn
+++ b/media/gpu/v4l2/BUILD.gn
@@ -60,8 +60,9 @@ source_set("v4l2") {
     "vp9/vp9_v4l2_compressed_header_types.h",
   ]
 
-  # enable_av1_v4l2_decoder
-  if (use_av1_hw_decoder) {
+  # enable_av1_v4l2_decoder. The AV1 stateless controls are only in the
+  # kernel headers of ChromeOS sysroots; Linux sysroots predate them.
+  if (use_av1_hw_decoder && is_chromeos) {
     sources += [
       "v4l2_video_decoder_delegate_av1.cc",
       "v4l2_video_decoder_delegate_av1.h",
diff --git a/media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_stateful_video_decoder.cc b/media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_stateful_video_decoder.cc
index 5978d3f07c..8ad33bb903 100644
--- a/media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_stateful_video_decoder.cc
+++ b/media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_stateful_video_decoder.cc
@@ -392,14 +392,19 @@ void V4L2StatefulVideoDecoder::Initialize(const VideoDecoderConfig& config,
   const auto profile_as_v4l2_fourcc =
       VideoCodecProfileToV4L2PixFmt(config.profile(), /*slice_based=*/false);
 
-  // Allocate larger |OUTPUT_queue_| buffers for resolutions above 1080p.
+  // Allocate larger |OUTPUT_queue_| buffers for resolutions above 1080p, and
+  // above 4K (8K VR video at 60-100 Mbps has key frames over 4 MiB).
   // TODO(hnt): Investigate ways to reduce this size.
   constexpr size_t kMiB = 1024 * 1024;
   constexpr int kFullHDNumPixels = 1920 * 1080;
+  constexpr int k4KNumPixels = 4096 * 2160;
+  const int area = config.coded_size().GetArea();
   const size_t kInputBufferInMBs =
-      (config.coded_size().GetArea() <= kFullHDNumPixels) ? 2 : 4;
+      area <= kFullHDNumPixels ? 2 : (area <= k4KNumPixels ? 4 : 8);
+  // The stream's size, not 0x0: drivers that size their buffers from it,
+  // like Qualcomm's iris (Steam Frame), refuse VIDIOC_REQBUFS otherwise.
   const auto v4l2_format = OUTPUT_queue_->SetFormat(
-      profile_as_v4l2_fourcc, gfx::Size(), kInputBufferInMBs * kMiB);
+      profile_as_v4l2_fourcc, config.coded_size(), kInputBufferInMBs * kMiB);
   if (!v4l2_format) {
     std::move(init_cb).Run(DecoderStatus::Codes::kFailedToCreateDecoder);
     return;
@@ -516,12 +521,10 @@ void V4L2StatefulVideoDecoder::Decode(scoped_refptr<DecoderBuffer> buffer,
       decoder_buffer_and_callbacks_.push(std::move(a));
     }
 
-  } else if (VideoCodecProfileToVideoCodec(config_.profile()) ==
-             VideoCodec::kHEVC) {
-    NOTIMPLEMENTED();
-    std::move(decode_cb).Run(DecoderStatus::Codes::kUnsupportedCodec);
-    return;
   } else {
+    // VP8/VP9, and HEVC: the demuxer hands over whole access units (Annex B,
+    // parameter sets ahead of key frames), which stateful decoders take as
+    // they are (Qualcomm iris on the Steam Frame).
     decoder_buffer_and_callbacks_.emplace(std::move(buffer),
                                           std::move(decode_cb));
   }
diff --git a/media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_utils.cc b/media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_utils.cc
